  "body": "Found in the review of PR #1670 (#1664). The same point applies to PR #1663 (#1609).\n\n**What happens.** A Ramp entry with no entry ramp angle uses the links' ramp angle (`links.ramp_angle`). This is the angle of the ramps between passes. When a user sets a large link angle, for example 45°, the entry ramp also becomes 45°. A steep chord is then kept at the cutting feed. The ramp angle of the entry and the ramp angle of the links are two different settings in practice.\n\n**Expected.** The Ramp entry has its own angle, with a safe default (3°). The links keep their angle. Alternatively, the entry uses the smaller of the two angles.\n\n**Done means:** the entry angle of Contour (side Inside), Circular and Bore does not follow a large link angle. A pin shows that a 45° link angle gives an entry at no more than the entry angle.\n",
